# Google's "Desktop application" OAuth client secret, used only for the desktop app's native Google sign-in
# (system-browser + loopback-redirect flow, see src/oauth.js). Google's own docs say this value isn't meant to
# stay hidden for this specific client type (every installed copy of every app using this pattern ships it) -
# but this value is never typed in by Claude, only by you:
#   - Local dev/testing: copy this file to apps/desktop/.env and paste the secret in.
#   - Released builds: add it as a GitHub Actions repository secret named GOOGLE_DESKTOP_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET
#     (repo Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions) - release-desktop.yml reads it from there and bakes it
#     into the build via scripts/prepare-oauth-secret.js before packaging.
GOOGLE_DESKTOP_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
